\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture of the proposed MMSAR evaluation framework. Synchronized RGB and thermal streams (illustrated via the 6$\times $2 environment gallery) are decimated to an 8~Hz timebase ($T_s = 125$~ms) and processed by parallel lightweight YOLO11n backbones. A common confidence cue $s[n] = \max (c_{\text  {RGB}}[n], c_{\text  {Thermal}}[n])$ is distributed across five competing causal temporal post-processing methods ($W = 5$ frames / 625~ms latency bound). Binary alarms are asserted against validation-optimized thresholds $\tau _m^*$ and evaluated across detection reliability and resource overhead.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_architecture}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
